                <pb facs="0319" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg247"/>

                <head>No. 16.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 14, 1881</date>.
                        (Received November 15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    reception of your lordship’s letter of the 11th instant, acquainting me with the
                    release from Kilmainham prison of Mr. Joseph B. Walsh, and inclosing,
                    confidentially, the order for his discharge. I shall not fail to communicate, by
                    an early opportunity, this information to the Department of State.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
